%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% expect-output: true
% expect-output: /undefined
% Scenario: a pattern instance across save and restore. An instance
% made before save, set and painted with inside it, is the current
% colour again once set after restore and paints from the cell the
% page already captured: one pattern resource, two fills. An instance
% made inside save lives in local VM and is discarded by restore with
% every reference to it, so the name it was defined under is undefined
% afterwards.
/P << /PatternType 1 /PaintType 1 /TilingType 1 /BBox [0 0 10 10]
  /XStep 10 /YStep 10 /PaintProc { pop 0 0 5 5 rectfill } >> matrix makepattern def
save
P setpattern
100 100 200 100 rectfill
restore
P setpattern
100 300 200 100 rectfill
currentcolor P eq =
save
/Q << /PatternType 1 /PaintType 1 /TilingType 1 /BBox [0 0 10 10]
  /XStep 10 /YStep 10 /PaintProc { pop 0 0 5 5 rectfill } >> matrix makepattern def
restore
{ Q setpattern } stopped { $error /errorname get == } if
showpage
